{"paper": "2024-Tier1-24-Sep-2024-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "155", "added": false}, {"text": "80", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "The following table gives zone wise survey report of the people of a country who take tea. Study the table and answer the question. The ratio of the total number of people surveyed who take tea more than 3 times a day to the number of people who do not take tea at all is", "options": [{"text": "103 : 8", "added": false}, {"text": "8 : 103", "added": false}, {"text": "101 : 5", "added": false}, {"text": "5 : 107", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "80 : 79", "added": false}, {"text": "80 : 71", "added": false}, {"text": "71 : 80", "added": false}, {"text": "79 : 80", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "The radii of two circles are 8 cm and 15 cm.The perimeter of the circle having area equal to the sum of the areas of the two circles (in cm) is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "Ghanshyam is thrice as old as Akash. 10 years ago, Ghanshyam was four times as old as Akash. What is the difference between their current ages (in years)?", "options": [{"text": "65", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}, {"text": "55", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "present-age", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "60", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}, {"text": "80", "added": false}, {"text": "70", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "An article is sold for₹747 after successive discounts of 17% and x%. If the marked price of the article is₹1,600, what is the value of x?", "options": [{"text": "32.26", "added": false}, {"text": "43.75", "added": false}, {"text": "22.12", "added": false}, {"text": "40.28", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "Two goods trains 132 m and 108 m in length are running towards each other on parallel tracks. The first train is running at a speed of 32 km/h and the second at a speed of 40 km/h. How much time will they take to cross each other after meeting?", "options": [{"text": "12 s", "added": false}, {"text": "10 s", "added": false}, {"text": "13 s", "added": false}, {"text": "15 s", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "On dividing a number by 55, we get 28 as the remainder. On dividing the same number by 11, what is the remainder?", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "Vipul spends 30% of his monthly income on rent, 60% of the remaining on groceries, and 40% of the remaining on others. If he saves ₹ 7056 in a month, then how much (in ₹) does he spend on groceries?", "options": [{"text": "18323", "added": false}, {"text": "15230", "added": false}, {"text": "17640", "added": false}, {"text": "22386", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "A man buys 10 kg of wheat at a rate of ₹26/kg. The wheat is mixed with 6 kg of other good quality of wheat to get a mixture at a price of ₹35/kg. The price of good quality wheat per kg (in ₹) is:", "options": [{"text": "38", "added": false}, {"text": "42", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}, {"text": "46", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixture-Alligation", "sub": "alligation", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "What is the length (in cm) of each side of a cube if the volume of a cube is 13,824 cm3?", "options": [{"text": "20.4", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}, {"text": "34", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "50", "added": false}, {"text": "45", "added": false}, {"text": "65", "added": false}, {"text": "75", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "If the mean proportional between p and q is 12, then the possible values of p and q, respectively, are:", "options": [{"text": "3, 38", "added": false}, {"text": "3, 28", "added": false}, {"text": "24, 6", "added": false}, {"text": "24, 16", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "The radii of two concentric circles are 26 cm and 10 cm. If the chord of the greater circle is a tangent to the smaller circle, then find the length of that chord.", "options": [{"text": "38.7 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "28.7 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "48 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "28 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "A person purchased a table and a sofa for ₹28,000. He sold the sofa at a profit of 10% and the table at a profit 15.25%. If his total profit was 13%, then the difference between the cost price of the sofa and the table (in ₹) is:", "options": [{"text": "1500", "added": false}, {"text": "4000", "added": false}, {"text": "5000", "added": false}, {"text": "2500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "A cell phone is available for Rs.600 or for Rs.300 cash down payment together with Rs.360 to be paid after two months. Find the rate of interest charged under this scheme.", "options": [{"text": "60%", "added": false}, {"text": "120%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "50%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "Let C be a circle with centre O and PQ be a minor arc on C. Let R and S be two points on the major arc of PQ on C. If PQ subtends an angle 80° at O, find ∠ PRQ and ∠ PSQ, respectively.", "options": [{"text": "40° and 60°", "added": false}, {"text": "50° and 80°", "added": false}, {"text": "40° and 40°", "added": false}, {"text": "40° and 50°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "For what value of K does the following system have an infinite number of solutions? x + 2Ky - 8 = 0 2x - y - 16 = 0", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "46", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "42", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}]}